    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d515">

                <pb facs="0521" n="511" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg511"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/1314: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-07T14:00:00-04:00">September 7, 1941—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>768. Your telegram 1110 of August 19.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d515-f1"/> The Navy
                    Department is becoming increasingly insistent as to the vital necessity of
                    obtaining the patrol plane facilities requested in the Department’s telegram 551
                    of July 17.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d515-f2"/> It cites such factors as the
                    protection afforded Hemisphere north-south shipping, the surface vessel needs
                    for its gigantic patrolling task (North and South Atlantic, Caribbean, far-flung
                    areas <pb facs="0522" n="512" xml:id="pg512"/> in the Pacific, etc.)—not to
                    speak of fleet operations—the relatively greater efficiency in certain patrol
                    tasks of planes over vessels, the effect of relieving surface vessel shortages
                    by use of planes when feasible; and mentions the President’s personal interest
                    and concern.</p>
                <p>The Department, recalling President Vargas’ anxiety at the “concentration” of
                    naval units in the Pacific at the expense of the Atlantic (paragraph 2 of your
                    telegram 425 of May 7, 7 p.m.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d515-f3"/>) and the repeated
                    assurances by the President and other high Brazilian officials of defense
                    cooperation, is likewise anxious that you endeavor to work out satisfactory
                    arrangements.</p>
                <p>In view of the above please furnish your considered views as to the probable
                    reaction of the Brazilian Government to a formal proposal along these
                        lines.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d515-f4"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
